sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant H as Host CPU
    participant D as GPU driver
    participant HBM as GPU memory
    participant SM as Streaming multiprocessors
    H->>D: copy input data to the device
    D->>HBM: DMA over PCIe
    H->>D: launch a kernel — a grid of blocks
    D->>SM: place each block on a free SM
    SM->>SM: split the block into warps of 32 threads
    loop every cycle
        SM->>HBM: fetch operands
        SM->>SM: all 32 threads run the same instruction
    end
    Note over SM,HBM: thousands of threads in flight hide memory latency — that is the whole trick
    SM->>HBM: write results
    H->>D: copy results back
